# The build stage runs `COPY . .`, so this file is the boundary between the repo and the image.
# Two things it protects:
#  - Secrets: without the .env exclusions, a populated .env is baked into image layers.
#  - The build cache: any file listed here can change without invalidating the COPY layer, so
#    editing .env no longer re-runs the entire 170-second build.

.git
.github

node_modules
**/node_modules

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

**/.next
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.mail
data
docs
*.md
!packages/providers/data/merchants/**/*.md

Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml
infra/caddy
